  "description": "Stage W2c (ARCHITECTURE decision 40): a service follows a running curve from call to call, x10 (one second a tick), on the track network: nodes a (512, 1536) to g (6656, 1536), a tile apart, joined by straight edges e1 a-b to e6 f-g, each 1024 long. Alpha (1536, 512), Beta (3584, 512) and Gamma (5632, 512) each have a platform on the half tile of track either side of their node, b, d and f: a train stops at the node going either way, and the far end of each platform is a berth too. setTrainPerformance checks the train, then that it runs no service, then the performance (a coast that does not slow less than the braking, or a top speed of 0, is invalidTrainPerformance); setLinePerformance checks the line, then the performance. A line plans each leg in the least whole second its performance builds a curve for, from whichever berth of its first stop gives the shortest round trip: for Express (Alpha, Gamma) that is Alpha's eastbound berth at the end of its east platform, 512 along e2, so the leg to Gamma is 3584 and the leg back to Alpha's node 4096. With the standard performance (1.5 and 2.5 km/h a second, 1/a + 1/b = 0.06 s\u00b2 a unit) they take sqrt(2 x 3584 x 0.06) = 20.7 and sqrt(2 x 4096 x 0.06) = 22.2 s, so 21 and 23, never reaching 110 km/h; with express (1.8 and 2.9 km/h a second, 0.050647) 19.05 and 20.4, so 20 and 21; with 2 minutes at each end 284 and 281 s, 5 minutes either way. Local has the metro game's performance (3.96 and 4.68 km/h a second: 70.4 and 83.2 units a second\u00b2, 80 km/h), stands at Alpha at the end of e1 and runs Alpha 0/1, Beta 2/2, Gamma 2/4 turning round, Alpha 10/10 (minutes). Started at 0, it dwells at Alpha (doors open by 8, closing from 51) and leaves at 60. Run 1 takes the 60 s its timetable gives it, from the scheduled departure to the scheduled arrival: {start 60, length 2048, seconds 60}, at Beta (the end of e3) at 120, on time. Beta is between the ends: least dwell 36 s, it leaves at 156, 36 s late. Run 2 is given 0 s, which no curve fits, so it takes the least, sqrt(2 x 2048 x 0.026224) = 10.4, so 11 s: {156, 2048, 11}; it accelerates for about 4 s, so 1 and 3 s after leaving it has come a x t\u00b2 / 2 = 35.2 and 316.8 units, 35 and 316 along e4; it reaches Gamma (the end of e5) at 167, 47 s late, lateness 37 a second after leaving (late since 120). Held at Gamma with a rate of 0, it still leaves at 240 (doors closing from 231), turned round to face west (e5 backward, at f; its path e4, e3, e2 backward to Alpha's node), and as it cannot follow its run {240, 4096, 360} (10 units along after a second) it drops it at once: a travelling service with no run. Given its rate back at 600, it sets off from a stand over the way left, 4096, as fast as it can: sqrt(2 x 4096 x 0.026224) = 14.7, so 15 s, {600, 4096, 15}; 35 and 316 units after 1 and 3 s again; at Alpha (the end of e2 backward) at 615, 15 s late, where its service ends at 657 (least dwell 42 s at the last stop: closing from 648). Balance 1,000,000 less 6 edges of a tile at 1,000, 3 stations at 50,000 and the train at 200,000.",
